  "starterCode": "# Load Balancing — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(assignments, num_experts):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Load Balancing** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(assignments, num_experts):\n    a=np.asarray(assignments,dtype=int).ravel()\n    if num_experts<1 or np.any(a<0) or np.any(a>=num_experts): raise ValueError(\"invalid expert assignment\")\n    counts=np.bincount(a,minlength=num_experts)\n    return {\"counts\":counts.tolist(),\"fractions\":(counts/max(1,len(a))).tolist()}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
